# LeakSanitizer suppressions for make unit-test-asan.
#
# ManagementActions::register_actions() (components/home_io_control/management_actions.cpp)
# registers native-API service descriptors with the ESPHome APIServer singleton once at
# setup(), transferring ownership to it — the same register-once/own-forever pattern
# ESPHome's own component APIs use throughout (e.g. api::APIServer::register_user_service()
# itself never frees what's registered). Real firmware never exits, so there is no leak in any
# operational sense; the host test binary does exit, so LeakSanitizer flags the still-reachable
# allocations made during each test's register_actions() call. Narrowly scoped to that one
# function rather than suppressed wholesale — see analysis/refactoring_p1_implementation.md
# "Findings" section for the ASan/UBSan triage this came out of.
leak:esphome::home_io_control::ManagementActions::register_actions
#
# Lr1121FirmwareUpdateController::run_boot_time_bootloader_read() allocates the LR1121 updater once
# at setup() and keeps it for the life of the firmware (every later bootloader/firmware action
# reuses it). Real firmware never exits, so nothing leaks operationally; the host test binary does
# exit, so LeakSanitizer flags it in any test that runs a full setup() with a BUSY pin wired (the
# host build always compiles the LR1121 feature in). Not freed in a destructor because the
# controller's tests point the same member at stack-owned updaters. Narrowly scoped to that one
# function, same as the register_actions() entry above.
leak:esphome::home_io_control::Lr1121FirmwareUpdateController::run_boot_time_bootloader_read
